z$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $9{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a64d7fd-d80f-53bd-910a-60419647eb47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566207 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+8\\cdot {0}^{2}-4{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $xz$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71858" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its $y$-intercepts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6548717-af2d-5bfc-9298-8a16a46973b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566269 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 1+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=0$ and $y=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
